  "viewports": [
    {
      "name": "desktop",
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 800,
      "capture_routes": [],
      "why_capture_routes_is_empty": "The desktop photographs of `login` and `not_found` are taken by `capture-regions.spec.ts` (artifacts under `regions/`), and they are what `published-screens.json` publishes. This project proves the other five reachable routes by marker instead. Unchanged from before the mobile pass."
    },
    {
      "name": "mobile",
      "width": 390,
      "height": 844,
      "capture_routes": [
        "login",
        "not_found"
      ],
      "why_capture_routes_is_these_two": "EXACTLY the two declared screens the desktop pass publishes, so mobile and desktop coverage stay 2 of 31 each. A wider mobile set would give screens a mobile image with no desktop sibling — an asymmetry the viewer switcher (T3) was built for the OTHER direction and would render as a dead desktop button. Widening it is a change to THIS array, not to the suite."
    }
  ],
  "marker_by_viewport": {},
  "min_regions_by_viewport": {},
  "provenance": {
    "routes": "measured — scripts/ux-capture/prepass.mjs, no model in the loop",
    "states": "opencode-go/qwen3.7-max + @playwright/mcp, ONE bounded session, 2026-08-13, 55 browser tool calls, ~5.5 min wall clock. Every entry below was re-verified deterministically before it was written here; the ones that did not survive are in e2e/support/capture-manifest.REJECTED.md.",
    "viewports": "measured — `node scripts/ux-capture/prepass.mjs --viewport mobile`, 2026-09-02, no model in the loop. The 390x844 prepass FLAGGED ZERO of the 31 routes: same reachability, same landing path, same visible stamped-region count, same `data-testid` set and the same `h1` on every single route. That is why `marker_by_viewport` and `min_regions_by_viewport` are EMPTY — there is nothing to override, not \"we did not look\". The fields exist so that the first route which does need an override is a DATA change and not a code change, and so that the override is a value a human chose rather than a number a script wrote. A marker is an anti-impersonation proof; the prepass may PROPOSE one, it may never COMMIT one.",
    "viewport_overrides_are_vacuous_today": "⚠️ Read the emptiness honestly: \"every flagged route has a committed override\" is TRUE BY CONSTRUCTION while the flagged set is empty. The assertion that is NOT vacuous is the marker-uniqueness one in `capture-manifest.spec.ts`, which runs at every viewport in `viewports` and checks each reachable route against the marker of every OTHER reachable route.",
    "viewports_remeasured": "`prepass.mjs` desktop vs `--viewport mobile`, 2026-09-22: 2 of 31 routes flagged, `signup` and `subscribe` (redirects to /signup), on `stampedVisible` only (44 -> 37). Cause: `SubscriptionIncludesPanel` swaps the desktop side panel for a compact list below `lg`. Marker and `min_regions` (13) still hold at 390, so no override is committed.",
    "mobile_states": "T5, 2026-09-22: 5 mobile-only candidates in `e2e/support/capture-candidates.mobile.json`, 0 promoted. Every one is accounted for in `capture-manifest.REJECTED.md`."
  },
